Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter. They asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
"Yes, he does that," he answered. And when Peter entered the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "On whom do kings of the earth take tolls and taxes? Do they take them from their sons or from others?"
"From others," Peter answered. Jesus said to him, "Then the children ought not to pay."
But we don't want to anger them. So go to the lake and cast your fishing line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. There you will find exactly the coin you need. Take it and give it to them as a tax for you and me.
